Send events, inspect how they metered, and drive the Flexprice API from your terminal.

Start with: flexprice init

Usage:
  flexprice [flags]
  flexprice [command]

Setup
  config                  Manage profiles
  env                     Inspect environments
  init                    Set up the CLI (guided)
  login                   Store credentials for a region and environment
  logout                  Remove a stored profile and its key
  open                    Open Flexprice in your browser
  version                 Print the CLI version and embedded spec build
  whoami                  Show the active profile, environment and key backend

Core billing
  checkout                Hosted checkout sessions
  customers               Manage the people and organisations you bill
  invoices                Draft, finalize and void billing documents
  payments                Payment attempts and their outcomes
  subscription-line-items Individual charges on a subscription
  subscription-schedules  Planned future changes to a subscription
  subscriptions           Active plan assignments and their lifecycle

Usage & metering
  costs                   Cost sheets derived from usage
  entitlements            What a customer's plan grants them access to
  events                  Raw usage events you send in for metering
  features                Capabilities that can be metered or gated

Credits & discounts
  coupon-associations     Which coupons apply to which subscriptions
  coupons                 Discount codes and their rules
  credit-grants           Prepaid and promotional credit allocations
  credit-notes            Refunds and credit memos against invoices
  wallets                 Prepaid credit balances held by a customer

Catalog & pricing
  addons                  Optional extras attachable to a plan
  plans                   Pricing models customers can subscribe to
  price-units             Units of measurement used by prices
  prices                  Individual pricing units within a plan
  tax-associations        Which tax rates apply to which entities
  tax-rates               Tax rates available to apply

Platform
  environments            Isolated spaces within your tenant
  groups                  Collections of users or entities
  integrations            Connections to Stripe, HubSpot and others
  rbac                    Roles and permissions
  secrets                 API keys and integration credentials
  tenants                 Your top-level account
  users                   People with access to your tenant

Automation
  alert-settings          How and when alerts fire
  alerts                  Threshold and anomaly notifications
  scheduled-tasks         Work queued to run later
  tasks                   Background jobs and their status
  workflows               Long-running billing processes

Advanced
  completion              Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  delete                  Issue a raw DELETE against the API
  get                     Issue a raw GET against the API
  help                    Help about any command
  post                    Issue a raw POST against the API
  resources               List every resource this CLI can act on

Flags:
      --all               page through every record (prints the last page; use --output json with --limit for bulk export)
      --api-key string    API key (CI use; prefer flexprice login)
      --base-url string   override the API base URL
      --columns strings   columns to show in table output
      --debug             dump requests and responses, secrets redacted
  -h, --help              help for flexprice
      --limit int         maximum records to return (default 20)
      --no-color          disable coloured output
      --no-input          never prompt; fail instead of asking
      --output string     output format: table, json, yaml (default "table")
  -p, --profile string    profile to use for this command
      --quiet             suppress progress output
      --region string     region key, e.g. us or in
  -v, --version           version for flexprice

Use "flexprice [command] --help" for more information about a command.
